WEBVTT

00:01.466 --> 00:02.467
KATARA: Water...

00:03.760 --> 00:04.928
Earth...

00:05.762 --> 00:06.888
Fire...

00:07.972 --> 00:09.224
Air.

00:10.099 --> 00:13.269
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:14.187 --> 00:17.941
Then everything changed
when the fire nation attacked.

00:18.691 --> 00:22.278
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

00:22.695 --> 00:25.907
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:26.407 --> 00:28.785
A hundred years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

00:29.702 --> 00:31.871
an airbender named Aang.

00:31.955 --> 00:34.082
And although his airbending
skills are great

00:34.165 --> 00:36.459
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:36.543 --> 00:37.544
AANG: Oof!

00:37.794 --> 00:41.422
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

00:41.548 --> 00:43.216
( OPENING MUSIC PLAYING )

00:47.136 --> 00:49.097
MAN: Previously on Avatar.

00:49.931 --> 00:52.559
WOMAN: Ember Island
is a magical place.

00:53.643 --> 00:55.770
TY LEE: Doesn't your family have
a house on Ember Island?

00:56.020 --> 00:58.856
AZULA: We used to come every summer
when we were kids.

00:59.440 --> 01:00.692
ZUKO: That was a long time ago.

01:01.442 --> 01:05.321
WOMAN: Like waves washing away
the footprints on the sand

01:06.030 --> 01:09.450
Ember Island gives everyone a clean slate.

01:09.993 --> 01:12.954
Ember Island reveals the true you.

01:19.335 --> 01:21.129
( BIRDS SQUAWKING )

01:32.599 --> 01:34.767
Doesn't it seem kind of weird
that we're hiding

01:34.851 --> 01:36.436
from the Fire Lord in his own house?

01:36.769 --> 01:40.398
I told you, my father hasn't come here
since our family was actually happy.

01:41.107 --> 01:42.358
And that was a long time ago.

01:42.650 --> 01:44.986
It's the last place anyone
would think to look for us.

01:45.320 --> 01:47.113
You guys are not
gonna believe this.

01:47.614 --> 01:48.990
There's a play about us.

01:49.657 --> 01:51.701
We were just in town,
and we found this poster.

01:52.243 --> 01:53.244
KATARA: What?

01:53.328 --> 01:54.871
How is that possible?

01:55.079 --> 01:56.080
Listen to this.

01:56.164 --> 01:57.832
"The Boy In The Iceberg is
a new production

01:57.915 --> 01:59.834
"from acclaimed playwright Pu-on Tin,

02:00.043 --> 02:02.962
"who scoured the globe, gathering
information on the Avatar.

02:03.338 --> 02:05.965
"From the icy south pole
to the heart of Ba Sing Se.

02:06.132 --> 02:09.010
"His sources include
singing nomads, pirates, prisoners of war

02:09.093 --> 02:11.596
"and a surprisingly knowledgeable
merchant of cabbage."

02:12.138 --> 02:14.599
SUKI: "Brought to you by the critically
acclaimed Ember Island players."

02:15.391 --> 02:16.392
Ugh.

02:16.684 --> 02:18.478
My mother used to
take us to see them.

02:18.728 --> 02:21.314
They butchered Love Amongst
The Dragons every year.

02:22.523 --> 02:24.400
Sokka, do you really think
it's a good idea

02:24.484 --> 02:26.527
for us to attend a play about ourselves?

02:26.986 --> 02:28.446
Come on.
A day at the theater?

02:28.655 --> 02:31.574
This is the kind of wacky,
time-wasting nonsense I've been missing.

02:35.328 --> 02:38.164
( GENERAL CONVERSATIONS )

02:43.461 --> 02:45.963
Hey, uh, I wanted to sit there.

02:46.297 --> 02:47.298
Just sit next to me.

02:47.382 --> 02:48.549
What's the big deal?

02:48.633 --> 02:50.843
I was just... I wanted to...

02:52.345 --> 02:53.596
Okay.

02:53.971 --> 02:56.224
Why are we sitting
in the nosebleed section?

02:56.391 --> 02:58.309
My feet can't see
a thing from up here.

02:58.476 --> 02:59.477
Don't worry.

02:59.560 --> 03:01.145
I'll tell your feet
what's happening.

03:01.813 --> 03:03.815
( MUSIC PLAYING )

03:08.111 --> 03:09.237
( GASPING )

03:10.279 --> 03:11.280
( SIGHING )

03:11.406 --> 03:13.199
Sokka, my only brother.

03:13.574 --> 03:16.661
We constantly roam
these icy south pole seas

03:16.869 --> 03:20.206
and yet, never do we find
anything fulfilling.

03:20.957 --> 03:23.501
All I want is a full feeling
in my stomach.

03:23.584 --> 03:24.627
I'm starving.

03:24.752 --> 03:26.421
( LAUGHING )

03:29.424 --> 03:31.801
ACTRESS KATARA: Is food the only
thing on your mind?

03:32.301 --> 03:35.680
Well, I'm trying to get it out
of my mind and into my mouth.

03:35.972 --> 03:37.056
I'm starving.

03:37.265 --> 03:38.266
( AUDIENCE LAUGHING )

03:38.349 --> 03:39.350
This is pathetic.

03:39.434 --> 03:41.352
My jokes are way
funnier than this.

03:41.477 --> 03:42.895
( LAUGHING )

03:42.979 --> 03:45.022
I think he's got you pegged.

03:45.565 --> 03:48.818
ACTRESS KATARA: Every day,
the world awaits a beacon to guide us,

03:48.985 --> 03:50.570
yet none appears.

03:50.653 --> 03:56.534
Still, we cannot give up hope,
for hope is all we have

03:56.617 --> 04:01.539
and we must never relinquish it, even...
Even to our dying breath.

04:01.748 --> 04:03.291
( SOBBING )

04:04.792 --> 04:06.002
Well, that's just silly.

04:06.085 --> 04:07.670
I don't sound like that.

04:07.795 --> 04:09.005
( LAUGHING )

04:09.088 --> 04:11.424
Oh, man, this writer's a genius.

04:15.928 --> 04:20.558
ACTRESS KATARA: It appears to be someone
frozen in ice, perhaps for 100 years.

04:20.933 --> 04:22.143
ACTOR SOKKA: But who?

04:22.351 --> 04:24.520
Who is the boy in the iceberg?

04:26.022 --> 04:27.023
Waterbend!

04:27.231 --> 04:28.232
Hi-ya!

04:33.696 --> 04:35.782
( CROWD "OOH"ING )

04:36.741 --> 04:39.160
Who are you, frozen boy?

04:39.744 --> 04:40.953
( LAUGHING )

04:41.037 --> 04:44.415
I'm the avatar, silly,
here to spread joy and fun.

04:45.124 --> 04:47.502
Wait, is that
a woman playing me?

04:48.795 --> 04:50.463
( GROWLING )

04:55.802 --> 04:56.803
( GASPING )

04:56.886 --> 04:58.471
An airbender.

04:58.721 --> 05:03.100
My heart is so full of hope
that it's making me tear-bend.

05:03.392 --> 05:05.645
( SOBBING )

05:06.979 --> 05:10.483
My stomach is so empty
that it's making me tear-bend.

05:10.691 --> 05:11.943
( SOBBING )

05:12.652 --> 05:13.861
I need meat!

05:14.153 --> 05:15.154
( GASPING )

05:15.238 --> 05:16.447
But wait.

05:16.531 --> 05:18.366
Is that a platter
of meaty dumplings?

05:18.950 --> 05:20.368
ACTOR SOKKA: Oh, where, where?

05:20.785 --> 05:22.495
( LAUGHING )

05:23.246 --> 05:26.165
Did I mention that I'm
an incurable prankster?

05:27.583 --> 05:29.043
I don't do that.

05:29.335 --> 05:30.461
That's not what I'm like.

05:30.670 --> 05:32.421
And I'm not a woman.

05:33.047 --> 05:34.048
( LAUGHING )

05:34.257 --> 05:36.634
Oh, they nailed you, twinkle-toes.

05:36.717 --> 05:37.760
( LAUGHING )

05:42.265 --> 05:44.851
Prince Zuko,
you must try this cake.

05:45.518 --> 05:47.645
I don't have time
to stuff my face.

05:47.770 --> 05:50.398
I must capture the avatar
to regain my honor.

05:50.940 --> 05:55.611
Well, while you do that, maybe
I'll capture another slice.

05:55.862 --> 05:56.904
( MAKING EATING NOISES )

05:56.988 --> 05:58.155
You sicken me.

05:58.573 --> 06:00.658
They make me look totally
stiff and humorless.

06:01.242 --> 06:03.995
Actually, I think
that actor's pretty spot-on.

06:04.537 --> 06:05.663
How could you say that?

06:06.163 --> 06:09.667
Let's forget about the avatar
and get massages.

06:10.167 --> 06:11.961
How could you say that?

06:18.843 --> 06:20.052
Hey, look.

06:20.136 --> 06:21.554
I think I found something.

06:25.892 --> 06:27.768
It's a flying rabbit monkey.

06:28.269 --> 06:30.187
I think I'll name him Momo.

06:30.396 --> 06:31.689
( LAUGHING )

06:32.690 --> 06:33.858
Hi, everybody.

06:34.066 --> 06:35.568
I love you.

06:36.736 --> 06:37.737
Ugh.

06:42.575 --> 06:44.994
Does this dress make
my butt look fat?

06:45.578 --> 06:46.954
( AUDIENCE LAUGHING )

06:49.457 --> 06:54.837
Riddles and challenges must you face
if you are ever to leave this place.

06:55.755 --> 06:57.089
( LAUGHING )

06:57.673 --> 06:58.841
( MOANING )

07:10.770 --> 07:13.481
ACTOR SOKKA: Why did you have to steal
that waterbending scroll?

07:14.690 --> 07:17.485
( SOBBING ): It just gave me
so much hope.

07:17.693 --> 07:19.070
( SOBBING )

07:23.699 --> 07:25.785
The avatar is mine!

07:25.993 --> 07:27.870
Wait, who's coming?

07:28.454 --> 07:32.792
MALE VOICE: I am the blue spirit,
the scourge of the fire nation

07:32.875 --> 07:34.502
Here to save the avatar.

07:40.967 --> 07:42.677
ACTOR AANG: My hero.

07:52.144 --> 07:53.521
( SOBBING )

07:55.314 --> 07:56.857
Don't cry, baby.

07:57.483 --> 08:00.319
Jet will wipe out
that nasty town for you.

08:05.658 --> 08:06.701
ACTRESS KATARA: Oh, Jet.

08:06.784 --> 08:08.285
You're so bad.

08:09.578 --> 08:10.746
( LAUGHING )

08:11.998 --> 08:17.336
Look, it's the great divide, the biggest
canyon in the earth kingdom.

08:19.588 --> 08:21.048
Eh, let's keep flying.

08:23.300 --> 08:24.802
Don't go, Yue.

08:25.011 --> 08:28.139
You're the only woman who's ever
taken my mind off of food.

08:29.807 --> 08:30.808
( GAGS )

08:30.891 --> 08:33.019
Wait. Did you have
pickled fish for dinner?

08:33.519 --> 08:34.729
Goodbye, Sokka.

08:34.937 --> 08:37.523
I have important moon duties
to take care of.

08:38.524 --> 08:41.986
And yes, I did
have pickled fish.

08:42.486 --> 08:43.571
( LAUGHING )

08:43.738 --> 08:45.573
You never told me you made out
with the moon spirit.

08:45.781 --> 08:47.992
Shh, I'm trying to watch.

08:57.168 --> 08:58.377
( LAUGHING )

08:58.461 --> 09:01.172
The avatar is back
to save the day!

09:01.255 --> 09:02.465
Yay!

09:08.512 --> 09:09.722
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

09:09.805 --> 09:10.931
-( GROANING )
-( LAUGHING )

09:18.481 --> 09:21.108
ZUKO: So far, this intermission
is the best part of the play.

09:21.609 --> 09:23.444
Apparently, the playwright
thinks I'm an idiot

09:23.527 --> 09:25.696
who tells bad jokes
about meat all the time.

09:26.030 --> 09:29.283
Yeah, you tell bad jokes
about plenty of other topics.

09:29.825 --> 09:30.951
I know!

09:31.243 --> 09:33.537
AANG: At least the Sokka actor
kind of looks like you.

09:33.829 --> 09:36.373
That woman playing the avatar
doesn't resemble me at all.

09:36.957 --> 09:37.958
I don't know.

09:38.042 --> 09:40.628
You are more in touch with
your feminine side than most guys.

09:40.878 --> 09:41.879
( GROANING )

09:41.962 --> 09:42.963
KATARA: Relax, Aang.

09:43.047 --> 09:44.340
They're not accurate portrayals.

09:44.840 --> 09:47.259
It's not like I'm
a preachy crybaby

09:47.343 --> 09:50.721
who can't resist giving overemotional
speeches about hope all the time.

09:53.140 --> 09:54.141
What?

09:54.308 --> 09:56.268
Yeah, that's not you at all.

09:56.769 --> 09:57.937
Listen, friends.

09:58.020 --> 10:00.397
It's obvious that
the playwright did his research.

10:00.981 --> 10:01.982
I know it must hurt,

10:02.066 --> 10:04.527
but what you're seeing up there
on that stage is the truth.

10:05.694 --> 10:08.656
Well, here we are
in the earth kingdom.

10:09.323 --> 10:13.285
I'd better have a look around to see
if I can find an earthbending teacher.

10:13.536 --> 10:14.578
This is it.

10:14.703 --> 10:16.330
This must be where I come in.

10:19.750 --> 10:21.877
ACTOR AANG: I flew all over town,

10:21.961 --> 10:25.631
but I couldn't find
a single earthbending master.

10:26.298 --> 10:27.341
Here it comes.

10:27.633 --> 10:30.594
You can't find an earthbending
master in the sky.

10:30.678 --> 10:32.346
You have to look underground.

10:32.721 --> 10:33.806
( LAUGHING )

10:34.265 --> 10:35.349
Who are you?

10:35.891 --> 10:40.563
My name's Toph, because it sounds like
tough, and that's just what I am.

10:40.646 --> 10:41.647
( AUDIENCE LAUGHING )

10:41.730 --> 10:42.731
Wait a minute.

10:42.815 --> 10:45.192
I sound like a guy.

10:45.609 --> 10:47.653
A really buff guy.

10:47.820 --> 10:49.947
Well, Toph, what you hear
up there is the truth.

10:50.322 --> 10:51.490
It hurts, doesn't it?

10:51.699 --> 10:52.908
Are you kidding me?

10:53.033 --> 10:54.869
I wouldn't have cast it
any other way.

10:55.327 --> 10:56.412
( LAUGHING )

10:56.495 --> 10:58.080
At least it's not
a flying bald lady.

11:00.958 --> 11:03.294
So, you're blind?

11:03.794 --> 11:04.920
( LAUGHING )

11:05.171 --> 11:06.755
I can see you doing that.

11:07.006 --> 11:10.718
I see everything that you see,
except I don't see like you do.

11:10.801 --> 11:13.012
I release a sonic wave
from my mouth.

11:14.096 --> 11:15.306
( SCREAMING )

11:20.394 --> 11:21.395
There.

11:21.478 --> 11:22.771
I got a pretty good look at you.

11:22.980 --> 11:24.190
( APPLAUSE )

11:27.443 --> 11:31.655
Zuko, it's time we had
a talk about your hair.

11:31.864 --> 11:33.741
It's gone too far.

11:34.116 --> 11:37.411
Maybe it's best if we split up.

11:41.373 --> 11:44.293
ACTOR ZUKO: Azula, my sister,
what are you doing here?

11:44.668 --> 11:45.878
You caught me.

11:46.128 --> 11:47.671
Wait, what's that?

11:47.963 --> 11:49.715
I think it's your honor.

11:49.924 --> 11:51.258
Where?

11:52.718 --> 11:53.928
She escaped.

11:54.011 --> 11:55.054
But how?

12:00.517 --> 12:04.230
If she continues drilling,
this wall will come down for sure.

12:06.565 --> 12:08.609
( LAUGHING ) Yes.

12:08.734 --> 12:10.444
Continue drilling.

12:10.861 --> 12:13.989
The city of Ba Sing Se
can hide no longer.

12:21.497 --> 12:22.706
( YAWNING )

12:30.547 --> 12:31.966
ACTOR AANG: No, Jet.

12:32.049 --> 12:33.634
What did they do to you?

12:34.218 --> 12:37.137
Must serve Earth King.

12:37.304 --> 12:38.389
( GASPING )

12:39.640 --> 12:42.351
Must destroy!

12:42.977 --> 12:44.895
( GRUNTING )

12:48.023 --> 12:50.025
Help. ( GRUNTING )

12:52.361 --> 12:54.405
Did Jet just die?

12:54.947 --> 12:56.782
You know, it was really unclear.

12:58.075 --> 13:02.705
I have to admit, Prince Zuko,
I really find you attractive.

13:03.205 --> 13:04.790
You don't have to
make fun of me.

13:05.499 --> 13:06.834
But I mean it.

13:07.001 --> 13:10.796
I've had eyes for you since
the day you first captured me.

13:12.798 --> 13:13.799
ACTOR ZUKO: Wait.

13:14.008 --> 13:15.968
I thought you were
the avatar's girl.

13:17.636 --> 13:18.637
( LAUGHS )

13:18.721 --> 13:19.722
The avatar?

13:20.222 --> 13:22.308
Why, he's like
a little brother to me.

13:22.391 --> 13:23.392
( LAUGHS )

13:23.475 --> 13:26.312
I certainly don't think of him
in a romantic way.

13:27.479 --> 13:31.317
Besides, how could he ever
find out about this?

13:33.861 --> 13:35.237
Oh, you're getting up?

13:35.612 --> 13:37.698
Can you get me some fire flakes?

13:39.700 --> 13:41.452
Oh, and fire gummies.

13:42.953 --> 13:47.207
Well, my brother,
what's it going to be?

13:47.416 --> 13:50.502
Your nation,
or a life of treachery?

13:53.380 --> 13:54.548
Choose treachery.

13:54.673 --> 13:56.258
It's more fun.

13:57.926 --> 13:59.511
No way.

14:02.473 --> 14:03.766
( GRUNTING )

14:03.849 --> 14:05.225
I hate you, uncle.

14:05.893 --> 14:08.687
You smell, and I hate you
for all time!

14:12.649 --> 14:14.360
You didn't really
say that, did you?

14:14.735 --> 14:16.195
I might as well have.

14:33.837 --> 14:36.090
( APPLAUDING )

14:37.174 --> 14:38.175
Avatar state.

14:38.258 --> 14:39.301
Yip-yip.

14:48.435 --> 14:50.521
Not if my lightning can help it.

14:52.481 --> 14:54.400
( SCREAMING )

15:00.823 --> 15:03.992
The avatar is no more.

15:05.411 --> 15:06.995
( CHEERING AND APPLAUDING )

15:12.668 --> 15:14.336
SUKI: It seems like every time
there's a big battle,

15:14.420 --> 15:15.963
you guys barely make it out alive.

15:16.213 --> 15:17.965
I mean, you guys lose a lot.

15:18.424 --> 15:19.758
You're one to talk, Suki.

15:19.842 --> 15:21.176
Didn't Azula take you captive?

15:21.427 --> 15:22.719
That's right, she did.

15:24.096 --> 15:25.973
Are you trying to get
on my bad side?

15:26.598 --> 15:27.724
I'm just saying.

15:28.100 --> 15:29.393
Does anyone know where Aang is?

15:29.726 --> 15:32.062
He left to get me fire gummies,
like, 10 minutes ago,

15:32.229 --> 15:33.730
and I'm still waiting.

15:34.731 --> 15:35.941
I'm gonna check outside.

15:46.285 --> 15:47.536
Are you all right?

15:47.703 --> 15:49.079
No, I'm not.

15:49.246 --> 15:50.539
I hate this play.

15:51.665 --> 15:54.543
I know it's upsetting, but it
sounds like you're overreacting.

15:54.877 --> 15:56.003
Overreacting?

15:56.295 --> 15:57.796
If I hadn't blocked my chakra,

15:57.880 --> 16:00.132
I'd probably be in
the avatar state right now.

16:03.385 --> 16:04.928
Whee!

16:06.054 --> 16:08.515
Suki, what are the chances
you can get me backstage?

16:08.765 --> 16:10.767
I got some jokes I want
to give to the actor me.

16:11.101 --> 16:16.315
I'm an elite warrior who's trained
for many years in the art of stealth.

16:17.608 --> 16:19.151
I think I could
get you backstage.

16:21.195 --> 16:24.156
Geez, everyone's getting
so upset about their characters.

16:24.364 --> 16:27.534
Even you seem more down than usual,
and that's saying something.

16:27.910 --> 16:28.952
You don't get it.

16:29.036 --> 16:30.245
It's different for you.

16:30.537 --> 16:33.790
You get a muscly version of yourself
taking down 10 bad guys at once

16:34.041 --> 16:35.501
and making sassy remarks.

16:36.043 --> 16:37.753
Yeah, that's pretty great.

16:37.961 --> 16:41.048
But for me, it takes
all the mistakes I've made in my life

16:41.173 --> 16:42.799
and shoves them back in my face.

16:43.425 --> 16:47.429
My uncle, he's always been on my side,
even when things were bad.

16:47.804 --> 16:49.014
He was there for me.

16:49.431 --> 16:52.309
He taught me so much,
and how do I repay him?

16:52.601 --> 16:54.102
With a knife in his back.

16:54.811 --> 16:58.398
It's my greatest regret, and I
may never get to redeem myself.

16:59.441 --> 17:01.485
You have redeemed yourself
to your uncle.

17:01.902 --> 17:04.112
You don't realize it,
but you already have.

17:04.488 --> 17:05.531
How do you know?

17:05.656 --> 17:08.283
Because I once had a long conversation
with the guy

17:08.450 --> 17:10.369
And all he would talk about
was you.

17:11.078 --> 17:12.079
Really?

17:12.162 --> 17:14.081
Yeah, and it was
kind of annoying.

17:14.540 --> 17:15.749
Oh, sorry.

17:15.832 --> 17:17.543
But it was also very sweet.

17:18.001 --> 17:21.672
All your uncle wanted was for you to find
your own path and see the light.

17:22.172 --> 17:23.382
Now you're here with us.

17:23.966 --> 17:25.217
He'd be proud.

17:26.343 --> 17:27.469
Ow.

17:27.928 --> 17:29.221
What was that for?

17:29.429 --> 17:31.014
That's how I show affection.

17:33.225 --> 17:36.645
Your Zuko costume's pretty good,
but your scar's on the wrong side.

17:38.480 --> 17:40.274
The scar's not on
the wrong side!

17:48.657 --> 17:50.075
He's coming this way.

17:52.119 --> 17:53.537
Can I help you?

17:53.912 --> 17:56.081
Actually, I think
I can help you.

17:56.540 --> 17:58.041
I'm a big Sokka fan

17:58.125 --> 18:00.335
but I don't think you're representing him
quite as well as you could be.

18:00.752 --> 18:01.837
Oh, no.

18:01.920 --> 18:03.338
Another fan with ideas.

18:03.422 --> 18:04.548
Just hear me out.

18:05.257 --> 18:07.301
Here's something I think
the real Sokka would say.

18:07.426 --> 18:08.427
( CLEARS THROAT )

18:08.510 --> 18:11.305
What does the cabbage merchant
use to fix his cabbages?

18:12.014 --> 18:13.640
A cabbage patch!

18:15.058 --> 18:16.226
( LAUGHING )

18:16.310 --> 18:17.394
That's actually pretty good.

18:17.519 --> 18:18.604
Let me see those.

18:20.063 --> 18:21.106
( LAUGHING )

18:21.189 --> 18:23.025
A rocky relationship.

18:23.108 --> 18:24.192
Not bad.

18:24.776 --> 18:28.780
Also, don't be afraid to make up some
phrases, especially before an attack.

18:28.989 --> 18:31.867
Something like,
"flying kick-a-pow!"

18:31.950 --> 18:33.452
ACTOR SOKKA: Who are you, anyway?

18:33.869 --> 18:35.579
I'm just a guy who likes comedy.

18:37.164 --> 18:39.499
Katara, did you really mean
what you said in there?

18:39.958 --> 18:41.209
In where?

18:41.293 --> 18:42.753
What are you talking about?

18:43.045 --> 18:46.882
On stage, when you said I was
just like a brother to you

18:47.257 --> 18:48.925
and you didn't have
feelings for me.

18:49.301 --> 18:50.344
I didn't say that.

18:50.469 --> 18:51.511
An actor said that.

18:52.095 --> 18:53.388
But it's true, isn't it?

18:53.930 --> 18:58.685
We kissed at the invasion, and I thought
we were gonna be together, but we're not.

18:59.436 --> 19:02.022
Aang, I don't know.

19:02.439 --> 19:03.690
Why don't you know?

19:04.024 --> 19:05.776
Because we're in
the middle of a war

19:05.859 --> 19:07.903
and we have other things
to worry about.

19:08.362 --> 19:09.780
This isn't the right time.

19:10.155 --> 19:11.865
Well, when is the right time?

19:12.908 --> 19:16.370
Aang, I'm sorry, but right now,
I'm just a little confused.

19:22.084 --> 19:23.794
I just said I was confused.

19:27.005 --> 19:28.340
I'm going inside.

19:31.218 --> 19:33.428
Ugh, I'm such an idiot.

19:38.975 --> 19:40.185
Here's what you missed.

19:40.352 --> 19:43.939
We went to the fire nation, and you got
better, and Katara was the painted lady

19:44.022 --> 19:46.900
and I got a sword,
and I think combustion man died.

19:47.025 --> 19:48.026
Ooh, look.

19:48.110 --> 19:49.611
The invasion's about to start.

19:49.695 --> 19:50.779
Shh.

19:51.405 --> 19:55.409
I just want to let you know,
Aang, that I'll always love you.

19:56.410 --> 19:57.911
Like a brother.

19:58.286 --> 20:01.123
I wouldn't want it
any other way.

20:11.800 --> 20:12.843
Hey, Toph.

20:12.926 --> 20:16.263
Would you say you and Aang
have a rocky relationship?

20:16.596 --> 20:17.597
( LAUGHING )

20:18.265 --> 20:19.391
( GASPING )

20:19.474 --> 20:21.017
I told him to say that.

20:22.185 --> 20:24.604
I hope everyone's ready
for the invasion.

20:24.980 --> 20:25.981
"Slop-a-pow!"

20:26.314 --> 20:27.315
( LAUGHING )

20:28.233 --> 20:30.610
( AUDIENCE LAUGHING )

20:34.531 --> 20:38.660
ACTOR AANG: We finally made it to
the royal palace, but no one's home.

20:39.244 --> 20:40.704
Actually, I'm home.

20:41.163 --> 20:42.539
And I want to join you.

20:43.790 --> 20:45.083
I guess we have no choice.

20:45.292 --> 20:46.334
Come on.

20:48.670 --> 20:49.921
I guess that's it.

20:50.005 --> 20:51.590
The play's caught up
to the present now.

20:51.715 --> 20:52.716
Wait.

20:52.841 --> 20:53.842
The play's not over.

20:54.134 --> 20:58.555
But it is over,
unless this is the future.

21:01.516 --> 21:03.643
With the energy harnessed from that comet,

21:04.060 --> 21:08.190
no one will be able to stop
the fire nation!

21:08.440 --> 21:11.401
Father, Zuko and the avatar
are at the palace.

21:11.777 --> 21:13.487
They are trying to stop you.

21:14.696 --> 21:16.364
You take care of Zuko.

21:16.531 --> 21:19.743
I shall face the avatar myself.

21:25.290 --> 21:27.918
Aang, you find the fire lord.

21:28.001 --> 21:29.419
I'll hold her off.

21:30.712 --> 21:32.964
You are no longer my brother.

21:33.173 --> 21:34.883
You are an enemy.

21:35.509 --> 21:39.346
No, I am the rightful heir
to the throne.

21:40.514 --> 21:42.432
We'll see.

21:54.569 --> 21:56.321
ACTOR ZUKO: Honor!

21:59.783 --> 22:02.202
( CHEERING AND APPLAUDING )

22:09.417 --> 22:13.088
So, you have mastered
all four elements?

22:13.839 --> 22:16.383
Yeah, and now,
you're going down.

22:17.384 --> 22:21.263
No, it is you
who are going down.

22:21.471 --> 22:23.807
You see, you are too late.

22:24.432 --> 22:29.563
The comet is already here,
and I'm unstoppable!

22:52.043 --> 22:53.879
No!

23:02.762 --> 23:04.222
It is over, Father.

23:04.389 --> 23:05.765
We've done it.

23:05.932 --> 23:08.643
Yes, we have done it.

23:09.185 --> 23:15.191
The dreams of my father and
my father's father have now been realized.

23:15.609 --> 23:19.154
The world is mine.

23:20.405 --> 23:22.574
( CHEERING AND APPLAUDING )

23:29.831 --> 23:32.208
ZUKO: That wasn't a good play.

23:32.500 --> 23:33.501
I'll say.

23:33.585 --> 23:34.586
No kidding.

23:34.669 --> 23:35.670
Horrible.

23:35.754 --> 23:36.755
You said it.

23:36.838 --> 23:38.048
But the effects were decent.

23:48.016 --> 23:50.977
( MEN VOCALIZING RHYTHMICALLY )
